--- du -s prints bytes ---
1892	big.txt
--- du -sh is human-readable ---
1.8K	big.txt
--- ls -l prints bytes ---
-rw-r--r-- 1 1892 big.txt
--- ls -lh is human-readable ---
-rw-r--r-- 1 1.8K big.txt
--- cp -v names the copy ---
'big.txt' -> 'copy.txt'
--- mv -v names the move ---
renamed 'copy.txt' -> 'moved.txt'
--- utility error is located in the bash mood ---
kosh: 1:1: error: cp: Not enough arguments.
     1 |  koshkit cp
       |  ^~~~~~~~~~
kosh: note: Try `cp --help` for more info.
--- and a missing operand is located in the bash mood ---
kosh: 1:1: error: ls: cannot access '/no/such/path': no such file or directory.
     1 |  koshkit ls /no/such/path
       |  ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
